cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TextFold in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "TextFold: Language Models as Reading Interfaces"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Xia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenxiachan/textfold"
url: "https://chenxiachan.github.io/textfold/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - human-AI interaction
  - reading interface
  - StretchText
  - semantic zoom
  - levels of detail
  - cognitive load
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  TextFold treats a language model as a reading interface rather than a
  summarizer. In the spirit of Nelson's StretchText, it folds a text into five
  levels of detail, from the full text down to a topic of a few words, and the
  reader moves between them to hold only as much of the text in mind as the
  task needs. The model decides what each level leaves out. The Brief level
  keeps the author's sentences verbatim, the written levels cite the sentences
  they rest on, and every paragraph opens back to the source. TextFold reads
  papers, web pages, PDFs, Office files, EPUB, Markdown and the replies of AI
  agents, and keeps the reader's highlights, notes and questions anchored to
  the passages they concern.
